
Ring x support: stop allocating the half of U3 that is identically zero.

K_vol = (K V_h) tbar^T sbar is rank one with two different supports: tbar is
the unsmoothed edge divergence, nonzero only on the U2 edge ring, while only
sbar carries the wide E A^c support.  The (support - ring) x (support - ring)
block that mastruct allocated is therefore identically zero.

fbares.py writes the U3 connectivity ring first and encodes nring in
lakon(3:3); mastruct.c and mafillsmas.f stop the outer loop at nring, and
e_c3d_u3 checks that tbar vanishes past it, naming the element and node
otherwise.  tests/verify_element.py checks the ordering and the label in the
deck.

VERIFIED: insertions fall ~3.3x at c = 1 (L_mesh 0.0240: 1.12e9 -> 3.4e8);
the 0.0240 deck's E_x is bit-identical to the dense-structure run of patch
0003; the patch test and confined compression are unchanged.


